# Notes stay LF on disk, whatever core.autocrlf says. context-mode's markdown chunker splits on
# "\n" and its heading regex fails on a trailing "\r", so a CRLF note is indexed as ONE chunk and
# loses every ranking (brain-doctor's vault-index check reports any CRLF note).
*.md text eol=lf
*.jsonl text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf

# Hook-written records travel between the boots by syncRecords (brain-lib). Both boots append to
# the same daily log, ledger and month indexes, so a rebase would conflict on every shared day; a
# union merge keeps both sides' lines. Commit notes are one file each and never collide.
30-Sessions/**/*.md merge=union
50-Ops/decisions.jsonl merge=union
50-Ops/Commits/commits-*.md merge=union
50-Ops/Health/*.md merge=union
50-Ops/Usage/*.md merge=union
50-Ops/00-MOC-Ops.md merge=union
